{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788973238,"nonce":"si+63ZEIsHC9rDIbd48WNfg5CeE=","title":"Found while implementing `eb35e1a` (`nepo-restock`), read-only against `nepo/Source/` and `Source/AutoRimmer/NepoBridge.cs`.","message":"`nepo-inbound` reports `pendingDispatches` as one undifferentiated list, and `Nepo/NepoGameComponent` fills that list from **two** sweeps, not one:\n\n* `RunRestockSweep` — a standing restock rule fired. The agent can now cause and read these (`nepo-restock`).\n* `RunSurgeryOrderSweep` — a pending surgery bill is missing a *fixed* ingredient (a bionic, a prosthetic, a drug), so Nepo orders it. Gated on `Config.autoOrderSurgeryItems`, and on nothing the agent can see.\n\n`Nepo/PendingDispatch` carries `def`, `count`, `stuff`, `color` and **no origin flag**, so the two are indistinguishable from the row. That leaves exactly the defect `eb35e1a`'s premise named, one surface over: an agent that has just listed every standing rule with `nepo-restock` can still see a dispatch matching none of them, with nothing in the reply able to explain it.\n\nThe fix is one config field. `NepoBridge` binds five of `NepoConfig`'s flags (`unlimitedMoney`, `instantDelivery`, `allowSlavePurchases`, `allowMinifiableBuildings`, `requireCommsForRestock`) plus the two allowance numbers. `autoOrderSurgeryItems` (`NepoConfig.cs` line 42, `public bool`, defaulted from `NepoSettings.DefaultAutoOrderSurgeryItems`) is not among them, so `mode` cannot say whether the surgery sweep is even running.\n\nNot urgent and not blocking: `nepo-inbound` is honest about what it reports, and its `dispatches.basis` already names both sweeps in prose. What is missing is the machine-readable half.\n\n\n- `NepoBridge` binds `NepoConfig.autoOrderSurgeryItems` in the READ tier alongside the other five flags, by name and type, so a rename disables the reads rather than throwing.\n- `NepoMode` carries `auto_order_surgery_items` and a `surgery_meaning` sentence naming `NepoGameComponent.RunSurgeryOrderSweep` as its only call site and saying it orders *fixed* recipe ingredients only (a multi-def filter like medicine's is deliberately out of scope on Nepo's side).\n- `nepo-inbound`'s `dispatches` block says, in one sentence keyed on that flag, whether a dispatch matching no standing rule can be a surgery order on this bench.\n- With `autoOrderSurgeryItems` off, `nepo-inbound` says so and the agent can conclude every dispatch came from a restock rule.\n- No new write: this is a read of Dorian's own setting, and `NepoSync.SetConfig` stays the only sanctioned writer.\n- Bench: with a pending surgery bill missing its part and `autoOrderSurgeryItems` on, advance past a sweep tick (2,500) and confirm the dispatch appears with `mode.auto_order_surgery_items:true` explaining it.","files":null}]}